From e53cbf2c572c5658eb3e021d5c336a5326b98a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 353/488] soh: name the 18 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_bw.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 18 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bw/z_en_bw.c.

  * func_809CE884 -> EnBw_Land
    deduced, confidence HIGH: squashes the Torch Slug's scale back to round
    as it settles from a bounce, then hands off to the walking setup.

  * func_809CE9A8 -> EnBw_SetupWalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts the looping eyestalk-wave animation,
    arms a randomised wander timer and installs the walking action.

  * func_809CEA24 -> EnBw_Walk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the wandering action: it steers the slug over
    the floor on a wobbling path, tracks the player and picks the next
    behaviour when its timer expires.

  * func_809CF72C -> EnBw_SetupRearUp
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the eyestalk-raise animation with the
    aiming sfx and installs the rearing action.

  * func_809CF7AC -> EnBw_RearUp
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stretches the slug tall as it rears, then
    returns it to walking when the stretch runs out.

  * func_809CF8F0 -> EnBw_SetupLunge
    deduced, confidence HIGH: aims at the player, launches the slug forward
    and upward with the jump sfx and installs the lunging action.

  * func_809CF984 -> EnBw_Lunge
    deduced, confidence HIGH: carries the lunge through, bouncing the slug
    back off the player on a hit and stretching its body along the arc.

  * func_809CFBA8 -> EnBw_SetupFlipOver
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts the flailing animation with the reverse
    sfx and installs the upside-down action.

  * func_809CFC4C -> EnBw_FlippedOver
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rolls the slug onto its back and leaves it
    hopping helplessly, throwing dust on each landing.

  * func_809CFF10 -> EnBw_SetupFlipBack
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts the same flailing animation with the
    reverse sfx and installs the righting action.

  * func_809CFF98 -> EnBw_FlipBack
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rolls the slug back upright, fading its colour
    to normal, and returns it to the landing action once it touches down.

  * func_809D00F4 -> EnBw_SetupDie
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the death sfx, drops targeting and
    installs the dying action.

  * func_809D014C -> EnBw_Die
    deduced, confidence HIGH: flattens and fades the slug out over forty
    frames, then kills the actor.

  * func_809D01CC -> EnBw_SetupFreeze
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the ice timer and the freeze duration and
    installs the frozen action.

  * func_809D0268 -> EnBw_Frozen
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shifts the slug's colour toward blue while it
    is frozen and shivers it on a random cycle.

  * func_809D03CC -> EnBw_SetupStun
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stops the slug, arms the ice timer for an ice
    hit, plays the freeze sfx and installs the stunned action.

  * func_809D0424 -> EnBw_Stunned
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the colour-filter timer and then
    restores whichever behaviour the slug was in before it was stunned.

  * func_809D0584 -> EnBw_CheckDamage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: kills the slug when it falls into a hazard and
    otherwise turns each AC hit into the matching freeze, stun, flip or
    death reaction.

